Password cracking is the process of recovering plaintext passwords from hashed or protected forms using different techniques. In ethical hacking, this is done only on systems you own or have permission to test.

1. Why Password Cracking Matters

Weak passwords = easy compromise

Helps test password policies

Shows impact of hash leaks

Common in CTFs, labs (TryHackMe, HTB), audits

2. Password Storage Basics

Passwords are not stored as plain text. They are stored as hashes.

Common Hash Types
Hash	Used In
MD5	Old apps, weak
SHA1	Legacy systems
SHA256 / SHA512	Modern apps
NTLM	Windows
bcrypt	Linux, web apps
Kerberos	Active Directory

Hash ≠ Encryption (hashing is one-way)

3. Password Cracking Techniques
1️⃣ Brute Force Attack

Tries all possible combinations

Very slow

Used only for short passwords

Example:

hydra -l admin -P passwords.txt ssh 10.10.10.10

2️⃣ Dictionary Attack

Uses wordlists

Faster than brute force

Popular wordlists:

rockyou.txt

SecLists

crackstation

Example:

hydra -l admin -P rockyou.txt ftp://10.10.10.10

3️⃣ Hybrid Attack

Dictionary + rules

Adds numbers/symbols

Example:

hashcat -m 0 hash.txt rockyou.txt -r rules/best64.rule

4️⃣ Rainbow Table Attack

Precomputed hashes

Fast but limited

Ineffective against salts

4. Online vs Offline Cracking
🔴 Online Cracking

Login attempts on live service

Slow

Risk of account lockout

Tools: Hydra, Medusa

🟢 Offline Cracking

Crack stolen hashes

No lockouts

Much faster

Tools: Hashcat, John the Ripper

5. Tools Used in Password Cracking
🔹 Hydra

Online attacks (SSH, FTP, HTTP)

hydra -l user -P rockyou.txt ssh://10.10.10.10

🔹 John the Ripper

Simple & powerful

john --wordlist=rockyou.txt hashes.txt


Show cracked passwords:

john --show hashes.txt

🔹 Hashcat (GPU-based)

Very fast

hashcat -m 1000 -a 0 ntlm_hashes.txt rockyou.txt

6. Common Hash Modes (Hashcat)
Mode	Hash
0	MD5
100	SHA1
1000	NTLM
1800	SHA512
3200	bcrypt
7. Windows Password Cracking

Steps:

Dump hashes

secretsdump.py administrator@10.10.10.10


Crack NTLM

hashcat -m 1000 hashes.txt rockyou.txt

